What hacks have you found? I guess my first thought is some sort of snippet to run in the browser console, or an extension, that you can just run when using youtube itself that copies the yt-dlp command to downloads all the page's search results to your clipboard. Definitely a hack I'm just curious what else you've seen.   copy(
     'yt-dlp ' +
     [...document.querySelectorAll('ytd-video-renderer a#video-title')]
       .map(a => {
         const u = new URL(a.href);
         return `"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=${u.searchParams.get('v')}"`;
       })
       .join(' ')
   )

