Interesting experiments and differences between the browsers.Using the test:
    (async () => {
      const sleep = (ms) => new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, ms));
      for (let i = 0; i < 200; i++) {
        __walker.add();
        await sleep(10);
      }
    })();From the JavaScript console, on both Chrome and Safari.The animation is _way_ smoother on Chrome, but scrolling on that page becomes really painful.Safari, on the other hand, uses a lot more CPU to do the animation, and the FP of that animation drops dramatically as you change the number of lemmings from 10 -> 50 -> 100 -> 200. However scrolling the page remains smooth the entire time.

